Year = {2024},
Volume = {1120},
Pages = {464-475},
Note = {13th Computer Science Online Conference, CZECH REPUBLIC, APR 25-28, 2024},
Abstract = {The core of this paper is a proposal of a control and monitoring system
   of the production process using smart sensors and Edge Computing (EC)
   technology. A solution proposed in this work provides the possibility of
   obtaining a wider spectrum of information than a normal control. Using
   the Multilayer perceptron neural network (MPL) and EC a faster data
   collection can be achieved without limiting the computing capacity and
   transfer services of the server. Additional benefits include
   availability of indirect data in process control, higher level of
   security by data collection and transfer, and, on top of that, low cost
   of components used. The proposed system reflects the current state of
   technology in the field, reflects on actual forms of the collection and
   usability of data, and offers opportunities to improve the quality of
   process management in general. This proposal shows that through EC, we
   are able to process a large amount of data (Big Data) from a number of
   devices/sensors (within proximity to the data), which we can analyze and
   process in a relatively short period of time. Thanks to analyzes and the
   use of AI (Deep Learning), we are able to react to errors or bad
   equipment conditions ``Just in Time{''}.},
