   Learning Applications in Physical Design{''} {[}25]. Since then, despite
   considerable activity across both academia and industry, many R\&D
   targets remain open. At the same time, there is now clearer
   understanding of where AI/ML can and cannot (yet) move the needle in
   physical design, as well as some of the difficult blockers and technical
   challenges that lie ahead. Some futures for AI/ML-boosted physical
   design are visible across solvers, engines, tools and flows and in
   contexts that span generative AI, the modeling of ``magic{''} handoffs
   at flow interstices, academic research infrastructure, and the culture
   of benchmarking and open-source EDA.},
