Note = {Symposium in Low-Power and High-Speed Chips (COOL CHIPS), Tokyo, JAPAN,
   APR 17-19, 2024},
Abstract = {SLMLET is a low-power System-on-a-Chip (SoC), which is a promising
   device for edge computing. It consists of a RISC-V core and area-saving
   embedded Field-programmable gate arrays (eFPGA) blocks called Scalable
   Logic Module (SLM). This paper presents a fabricated SLMLET chip and a
   developed HW/SW co-design flow. The experimental results demonstrate
   that the RISC-V core can operate at up to 300MHz, and a hardware design
   on the SLM blocks can operate at up to 100MHz. By offloading
   compute-intensive processes to dedicated circuits implemented in the SLM
   blocks, it is possible to achieve up to 77 \% energy reduction compared
   to software processing on the RISC-V core and other commercial
   microcontrollers.},
