Note = {23rd International Conference on Trust Security and Privacy in Computing
   and Communications-TRUSTCOM-Annual, Sanya, PEOPLES R CHINA, DEC 17-21,
   2024},
Abstract = {The transformer has profoundly driven the development of natural
   language processing and computer vision tasks. However, their widespread
   deployment has raised concerns about the potential leakage of data
   privacy. To address the issue, homomorphic encryption (HE) is employed
   as a secure technique to process user private inputs over ciphertexts.
   As HE only supports linear operations, non-linear functions are required
   to be approximated into polynomials, which leads to heavy communication
   and computation overhead. In this paper, we propose THEF
   (Tee-and-HE-based Framework), an efficient and secure inference
   framework for transformer inference, which uses HE to ensure data
   security and leverages Trusted Execution Environment (TEE) to reduce
   communication and computation cost. We also design a number of
   optimization methods, including expanding encoding matrix multiplication
   scheme, batch acceleration and adaptive scheme, to improve performances
   of the THEF. Finally, we compare the performances of THEF and the
   state-of-the-art methods. The experimental results demonstrate that THEF
   maintains a level of accuracy close to that of plaintext model, reduces
   end-to-end communication cost by 80\% and achieves significant
   improvement in end-to-end run-time.},
