   CONFERENCE, ECTC 2024},
Series = {Electronic Components and Technology Conference},
Year = {2024},
Pages = {1085-1092},
Note = {IEEE 74th Electronic Components and Technology Conference (ECTC),
   Denver, CO, MAY 28-31, 2024},
Abstract = {In this paper, signal integrity (SI) performance has been investigated
   for advanced interconnect bridge on organic package (AIBO) technology.
   Performance comparison under various conditions- conductor roughness
   change, layers of routing, temperature difference has been conducted.
   This paper also introduces package power integrity (PI) analysis
   including DC IR drop, AC voltage droop studies and optimizations for
   advanced package. Power integrity (PI) challenges for high current
   consumption of FPGAs' core power rail are analyzed and enablement
   solutions on package level are proposed to meet noise specifications
   without additional costs. Under high power and high current condition,
   thermal integrity issue has been raised and temperature map is obtained
   to identify the hotspot on a package design.
   All these studies are essential to guarantee a successful package design
   to meet requirements of intensive computing, high data rate, low
   latency, higher current consumption working environments the new
   artificial intelligence (AI) era brings in.},
