   NETWORKING 2025, ICDCN 2025},
Year = {2024},
Pages = {289-294},
Note = {26th International Conference on Distributed Computing and Networking,
   Hyderabad, INDIA, JAN 04-07, 2025},
Abstract = {Today, remote computational activities must be secure and private.
   Trusted Execution Environments (TEEs) enable hardware-based data and
   operation isolation. This method may expose users to side-channel
   attacks and software exploits. This paper offers a new remote
   computation protocol that uses Algebraic Signatures (AS) to secure TEE
   systems. This research proposes an efficient, scalable, and secure
   AS-based TEE framework. This AS-based protocol is evaluated extensively
   to show that it is a top key generation, signa ture computation, and
   verification solution. After a security study finds the strengths and
   weaknesses of the protocol, appropriate optimizations improve
   performance and security.},
