Year = {2024},
Volume = {1113},
Pages = {43-53},
Note = {54th Meeting of the Italian Electronics Society, Noto, ITALY, SEP 06-08,
   2023},
Abstract = {To support quantized neural networks in low-end CPUs, we propose STAR
   MAC, a reconfigurable multiply-and-accumulate unit based on a modified
   Baugh-Wooley architecture that operates at a variable reduced precision.
   We integrated it in a small RISC-V processor called Ibex obtaining an
   acceleration up to 5.8x in Fully-Connected (FC) layers, 3.7x in
   2D-Convolution (2DConv) layers, and 2.8x in DepthWise Convolution
   (DWConv) layers, with respect to the original Ibex core (Orig.), and up
   to 4.5x in FC layers, 3.0x in 2DConv layers, and 2.3x in DWConv layers,
   against a modified Ibex core supporting standard 32-bit MAC operations
   (Orig.+MAC). Area and power in a 28-nm technology with 200 and 600 MHz
   target clock frequency are 0.015 and 0.017mm2, and 1.5 and 4.3mW,
   respectively, with a limited overhead within 10\% and 3\% with respect
   to Orig., and within 3\% and 3\% against Orig.+MAC.},
