   Bari, ITALY, JUL 14-18, 2024},
Abstract = {Research is underway on a new approach to indoor 6G networks that
   combines lighting, communication, and sensing. This technology, called
   integrated sensing, communication, and lighting, utilizes visible light
   communication (VLC) to transmit data through LED lights. VLC offers a
   vast unlicensed spectrum, high speed, and potential for improved
   security compared to traditional radio frequency communication. In
   addition to communication, VLC has been suggested for visible light
   positioning and sensing. In this paper we will discuss some major
   breakthroughs needed for integrated sensing, communication, and lighting
   (ISCL) for indoor 6G networks using visible light communication (VLC)
   like Improved Modulation Techniques, ML based radio mapping and Security
   Enhancements.<bold> </bold>},
