Note = {2024 China Automation Congress, Qingdao, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 01-03,
   2024},
Abstract = {At present, the tasks of robots are becoming increasingly diverse, and
   higher requirements have been put forward for the perception system of
   robots. Among them, tactile sensing is an indispensable part of the
   robot perception system. Therefore, it is necessary to design tactile
   sensors that are sensitive to the surface features of the object being
   grasped. This paper proposes a tactile sensor based on the theory of
   triboelectric nanogenerators. The sensor surface adopts a fingerprint
   like structure and can output different voltage signals by sliding on
   the surface of the object. The experimental results show that FP-TENG
   can provide different voltage signals when in contact with objects with
   different materials and surface structures. When this sensor is applied
   to detect rust, there is a significant difference in voltage signals
   when in contact with metals with different degrees of rust, providing a
   new research direction for tactile sensing in robotic hands.},
