   Bangalore, Bangalore, INDIA, FEB 22-24, 2024},
Abstract = {Verifying programs under weak memory models (WMMs) is vital due to their
   prevalence in modern computer architectures. These models introduce
   complexities, allowing unexpected reordering and visibility of memory
   operations. Ensuring correctness is crucial to prevent subtle bugs and
   guarantee the reliability of software running on such systems. However,
   a memory model specific technique cannot be extended to other memory
   models. In this work, we strive to develop an automated parameterized
   verification technique capable of analyzing programs under all possible
   WMMs.},
Type = {Proceedings Paper},
Affiliation = {Sharma, D (Corresponding Author), Indian Inst Technol Delhi, Delhi, India.
