Note = {42nd VLSI Test Symposium (VTS), Tempe, AZ, APR 22-24, 2024},
Abstract = {Modern machine learning (ML) applications are becoming increasingly
   complex and monolithic (single chip) accelerator architectures cannot
   keep up with their energy efficiency and throughput demands. Even though
   modern digital electronic accelerators are gradually adopting 2.5D
   architectures with multiple smaller chiplets to improve scalability,
   they face fundamental limitations due to a reliance on slow metallic
   interconnects. This paper outlines how optical communication and
   computation can be leveraged in 2.5D platforms to realize
   energy-efficient and high throughput 2.5D ML accelerator architectures.},
