Pages = {335-343},
Note = {13th Computer Science Online Conference, CZECH REPUBLIC, APR 25-28, 2024},
Abstract = {In the first part contribution presents the main approaches to the
   development of post-quantum algorithms and reviews progress in the field
   of quantum computers and post-quantum cryptographic encryption systems.
   Further, article considers the most promising approaches, that are based
   on the using of theory of lattices. Then, authors reviews in more detail
   the Goldreich Goldwasser Halevi encryption scheme based on the theory of
   lattices. In the second part, article presents a software package that
   allows the user to study the main functions of the GGH scheme: key
   generation algorithms, encryption algorithms and message decryption. The
   article specifies the main purposes of the modules of the software
   package, describes the user interface of the program. Also, the software
   package makes it possible to carry out an attack on the encryption
   scheme using the Lenstra-Lenstra-Lovasz algorithm. The article considers
   the details of applying this algorithm, mentioning the difficult to
   solve problems, which are being the base of cryptographic scheme and are
   being solved by LLL-algorithm. This application can be used as part of a
   laboratory complex when studying. \#CSOC1120.},
